# Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
artifacts/
*.user
*.suo

# Vixen project-local caches (never committed — reproducible from source + .meta).
# The negation is load-bearing: Raven/Library/ is the shipped .rvn standard library
# (docs/plan/02 § Raven), not a cache, and a bare `Library/` swallowed it. Example1.rvn
# and Example2.rvn were tracked only because they predate this rule — anything added
# beside them was invisible to git.
Library/
!Raven/Library/

# `Build/` used to be listed here, and it made the entire Nuke build project
# invisible to git: macOS and Windows match ignore patterns case-insensitively, so
# it swallowed `build/` — Build.cs, the architecture rules, _build.csproj, all of
# it. `build.sh` was tracked; the project it runs was not. Compiled output is
# already covered by [Bb]in/ and [Oo]bj/ above, so the line was buying nothing.

# A Vixen project's content-build output. Anchored to Samples/ rather than written as a
# bare `Build/`, for exactly the reason the paragraph above gives: macOS and Windows match
# ignore patterns case-insensitively, so an unanchored line swallows the Nuke `build/`
# project again. Bundles and a catalog are reproducible from the assets and their .meta.
Samples/*/Build/

# ANTLR: the IDE plugin's scratch dir, and the .tokens/.interp vocabularies.
# The build regenerates these into obj/ from the .g4 files; a committed copy only
# ever goes stale against the grammar.
.antlr/
*.tokens
*.interp

# CPython's bytecode cache, for the reason directly above: regenerated from a tracked source file,
# so a committed copy only ever goes stale against it. `Samples/13-ThirdPersonShooter/Content` is the
# only Python in the tree — content-generation scripts — and `gentex.cpython-313.pyc` rode in there
# on 64ac6069, a commit about a sampler, because nothing was ignoring it. Note which script:
# make_textures.py does `from gentex import ...`, so gentex.py is the one imported as a module and
# the only one CPython caches. The name carries the interpreter version too, so a tracked cache is
# dead weight on any machine not running 3.13.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.DotSettings.user

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test / coverage
TestResults/
*.trx
# Written beside a golden file when it does not match, for eyeballing the diff.
*.actual
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# Native deps restored by `nuke RestoreNativeDeps`
/native/

# Reference clones (see docs/plan/02 § references/) — local clones, not submodules.
# The README is tracked so the directory explains itself and carries the clone commands.
/references/*
!/references/README.md

# Nuke's generated schema and run logs, and BenchmarkDotNet's scratch
/.nuke/build.schema.json
/.nuke/temp/
/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# The documentation site's install and build outputs.
www/node_modules/

# The VS Code extension: its dependencies and its packaged output.
Tools/Vixen.VSCode/node_modules/
Tools/Vixen.VSCode/*.vsix
www/dist/
www/.angular/
www/out-tsc/

Trellis/

# Captures written by --vixen-capture. A picture that proved something belongs in a report or
# beside a golden, not in the sample it was taken from.
shots/
